\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 5. Tactical Communication Scripts\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 Use these adaptable templates to handle critical workplace interactions ethically and professionally:\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\li4620\fi-4620\ri4620\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 A. Seeking Feedback on Communication & Tone\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i\b0\fs24 \cf2 "I'm currently working on refining my leadership style, specifically ensuring my communication is clear, open, and constructive under tight deadlines. In our recent project, was there any point where my communication felt overly rushed, opaque, or sharp? I'd really appreciate your honest feedback so I can adjust."
\f1\i0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\li4620\fi-4620\ri4620\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 B. Pausing Before Reactive or Impulsive Decisions\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i\b0\fs24 \cf2 "I see the urgency here, and I know we want to move fast. However, I want to pause briefly to run a quick sanity check on the human and operational impacts before we finalize this direction. Let's take 10 minutes to review who this affects and make sure we aren't missing key risks."
\f1\i0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\li4620\fi-4620\ri4620\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 C. Publicly Sharing Credit & Highlighting Contributions\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i\b0\fs24 \cf2 "While I'm presenting this initiative today, the core breakthroughs came directly from [Colleague/Team Name]. Their analysis on [specific detail] was critical to getting us here, and I want to ensure their contribution is fully recognized."
\f1\i0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\li4620\fi-4620\ri4620\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 D. Repairing Interpersonal Harm or Tone Slippage\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i\b0\fs24 \cf2 "I want to touch base about my comment during earlier today. My tone was unnecessarily sharp, and it fell short of the respectful, open standard I set for myself. I apologize for how that came across, and I'm committed to ensuring our conversations remain constructive going forward."
\f1\i0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\li4620\fi-4620\ri4620\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 E. Responding Ethically to Workplace Conflict\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\i\b0\fs24 \cf2 "We clearly have different perspectives on how to proceed here. Rather than rushing to a decision, let's step back and look at what outcome serves the project and team best. What are your primary concerns with this approach, and how can we address them fairly?"
\f1\i0 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\li4620\fi-4620\ri4620\partightenfactor0

